      "content": "Yeah, the board is pretty adamant about it. They feel that the \"black box\" nature of probabilistic reasoning introduces too much unquantifiable risk into the safety chain. They want a system where every failure trigger is a clear, hard-coded logic gate. Basically, if they can't trace the exact \"why\" through a static rule, they don't want it in the cockpit loop. So, once the migration is complete, your current predictive protocols will be completely taken offline.",
